## Installation

This package is not published to a package index. Install it directly from
GitHub (requires read access to the repository):

```bash
uv add git+{{ repo_url }}
```

Pin to a released tag:

```bash
uv add git+{{ repo_url }}@v{{ initial_version if versioning_resolved == 'static' else '0.1.0' }}
```
{% if versioning_resolved == 'vcs' %}
> [!IMPORTANT]
> This package derives its version from git tags at build time.
>
> **Supported:** `git+https://` installs (a real clone, so tag history is
> present) and installs from a built sdist or wheel (the version is baked into
> the distribution metadata).
>
> **Not supported:** GitHub's auto-generated source archives, i.e.
> `{{ repo_url }}/archive/refs/tags/v1.0.0.tar.gz`. These are raw tree
> snapshots with no `.git` directory and no packaging metadata, so the build
> cannot determine a version and fails outright.
{% endif %}
