## Versioning and releases

{% if versioning_resolved == 'vcs' -%}
The version is derived from git tags via `hatch-vcs`; it is never written into
`pyproject.toml`. To release, tag the commit:

```bash
git tag v0.2.0
git push origin v0.2.0
```

Untagged builds get a development version such as `0.1.1.dev4+g1a2b3c`.
Because the version is dynamic, `uv version` cannot read or set it — read
`{{ package_name }}.__version__` from an installed copy instead.
{%- else -%}
The version is set statically in `pyproject.toml`. To release, bump it, then
tag the same commit so the two never disagree:

```bash
uv version --bump minor
git commit -am "chore: release v$(uv version --short)"
git tag "v$(uv version --short)"
git push --follow-tags
```
{%- endif %}

{% if changelog_tool == 'git-cliff' -%}
`CHANGELOG.md` is generated from Conventional Commits:

```bash
uv run poe changelog
```

Commit messages are the source of the changelog, so write them for a reader
who was not in the pull request.
{%- else -%}
`CHANGELOG.md` is maintained by hand, following
[Keep a Changelog](https://keepachangelog.com/). Add an entry under
`[Unreleased]` in the same pull request as the change.
{%- endif %}

## Updating from the template

This project was scaffolded from a Copier template and can pull in later
template changes:

```bash
uvx copier update --trust
```

Review the three-way merge carefully — local edits to templated files may
conflict. Never delete or hand-edit `.copier-answers.yml`.

